Kafka

Streaming 

Multiple machines and each machine is call broker
Producer —produce—> Topic <—consumes—consumer
Producer could be any API such as java api etc 


There are 2 types of communication:
1. Synchronus communication
2. Asynchronous commnunication - which doesn’t wait for response, example sending email. 


Kafak is used for Synchronous communication

2 kinds of communication:
1. pubSub
2. Point-to-point

1. PubSub- all consumers consumes all the messages produced by each producers?
	there’s only one partition 
	P -> [m1,m2,m3 ] <- C{c1,c2,c3}

2. Point-to-point - when there’s partitions and each producer produces to one partition and each consumer comumes from each partitions
Topic:
	m0 -> p0 <-c0
	m1 -> p1 <-c1
	m2 -> p2 <-c2




Interview questions:
	1. Suppose you have a topic that has partition, what are the ways to distribute in partition?
	-> 3 ways:
		a. Round robin fashion:
			producers:-> m0,m1,m2
			then message distribution within the partitions:  m0->p0
										m1 -> p1
										m2 -> p2
		and if there another message then it goes to p0		m3 -> p0
		b. Key- a producer can generate key to each message I.e, hashcode
			k0: m0 - hashcode(k0) = 0%3=0
			k1: m1 - hashcode(k1) = 1%3=1
			k2: m2 - hashcode(k2) = 2%3=2
		c. Passing partition while producer distributes the message

	2. Why do we need partitions?
	—> 


What happens when:
1. more consumers than partitions -extra consumers sits idle or used in place of broken consumer
2. Less consumers than partitions - one consumer is duty to read more than one partition, meaning one consumer can read more than one partition as of its capacity in case of insufficient consumers per partitions


Zookeeper - is a standalone service. It’s mostly used to create communication. 
		- to coordinate between multiple services
		- is a distributed coordination service


Machine1 —talk— machine2 : but not reliable
Thats where zookeepers comes in:
Machine1 — zookeeper — machine2 : reliable communication


What zookeeper does in Kafka?
Kafka can have multiple consumers and producers. 
Producer produces the message and in partition the messages are stored in order and consumer c

Zookeeper keeps the metadata of each message consumed by consumers from a partition
-> is responsible to elect leader machine/broker
Helps -> In fault-tolerant (when a consumer does down)


Zookeeper is responsible for leader election - helps in fault-tolarent 
Leader - is responsible for First copy and all the read and write
B1 	t1:p0	rt1:1	B1 is a leader for p0
B1 	rt1:p0	t1:1	B2 is a leader for p1
B1 	rt1:p0	rt1:1	

























